--- 3. the enforcing triggers and the functions they call
+------------------------------------------------+-----------------------+--------------------------------------+------------------+
|                     tgname                     |       on_table        |               function               | security_definer |
+------------------------------------------------+-----------------------+--------------------------------------+------------------+
| estate_enforce_out_of_term_billing_on_create   | estate_dues_invoices  | estate_enforce_out_of_term_billing   | f                |
| estate_enforce_vacant_unit_exemption_on_create | estate_dues_invoices  | estate_enforce_vacant_unit_exemption | f                |
| estate_enforce_unit_capacity_on_write          | estate_unit_occupants | estate_enforce_unit_capacity         | f                |
| estate_reset_proof_on_redeclaration_on_write   | resident_profiles     | estate_reset_proof_on_redeclaration  | f                |
+------------------------------------------------+-----------------------+--------------------------------------+------------------+
(4 rows)

--- 4. the single admitting/releasing writers must be SECURITY DEFINER and owner-only executable
+--------------------------+-----------+----------+------------------+
|         proname          | prosecdef |  owner   | non_owner_grants |
+--------------------------+-----------+----------+------------------+
| estate_occupancy_admit   | t         | postgres | EXECUTE,EXECUTE  |
| estate_occupancy_release | t         | postgres | EXECUTE,EXECUTE  |
+--------------------------+-----------+----------+------------------+
(2 rows)

--- 5. the two dues-exemption CHECKs and the proof-state CHECK are live constraints
+----------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                   conname                    |                                                  definition                                                   |
+----------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| estate_dues_invoices_term_override_reason    | CHECK (((NOT term_override) OR (btrim(COALESCE(term_override_reason, ''::text)) <> ''::text)))                |
| estate_dues_invoices_vacancy_override_reason | CHECK (((NOT vacancy_override) OR (btrim(COALESCE(vacancy_override_reason, ''::text)) <> ''::text)))          |
| estate_unit_occupants_occupancy_type_check   | CHECK ((occupancy_type = ANY (ARRAY['resident'::text, 'tenant'::text, 'homeowner'::text])))                   |
| estate_unit_occupants_window_ordered         | CHECK (((effective_from IS NULL) OR (effective_until IS NULL) OR (effective_until >= effective_from)))        |
| resident_profiles_proof_status_check         | CHECK ((proof_status = ANY (ARRAY['unverified'::text, 'pending'::text, 'verified'::text, 'rejected'::text]))) |
+----------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
(5 rows)

--- 5b. the one-owner / one-tenant overlap rule is a PARTIAL UNIQUE INDEX, not a table constraint
+-----------------------+-----------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|       tablename       |                   indexname                   |                                                                                        indexdef                                                                                        |
+-----------------------+-----------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| estate_unit_occupants | estate_unit_occupants_live_idx                | CREATE INDEX estate_unit_occupants_live_idx ON public.estate_unit_occupants USING btree (property_id) WHERE (ended_at IS NULL)                                                         |
| estate_unit_occupants | estate_unit_occupants_one_live_owner          | CREATE UNIQUE INDEX estate_unit_occupants_one_live_owner ON public.estate_unit_occupants USING btree (property_id) WHERE ((occupancy_type = 'homeowner'::text) AND (ended_at IS NULL)) |
| estate_unit_occupants | estate_unit_occupants_one_live_tenant         | CREATE UNIQUE INDEX estate_unit_occupants_one_live_tenant ON public.estate_unit_occupants USING btree (property_id) WHERE ((occupancy_type = 'tenant'::text) AND (ended_at IS NULL))   |
| estate_unit_occupants | estate_unit_occupants_pkey                    | CREATE UNIQUE INDEX estate_unit_occupants_pkey ON public.estate_unit_occupants USING btree (id)                                                                                        |
| estate_unit_occupants | estate_unit_occupants_property_id_user_id_key | CREATE UNIQUE INDEX estate_unit_occupants_property_id_user_id_key ON public.estate_unit_occupants USING btree (property_id, user_id)                                                   |
| estate_unit_occupants | estate_unit_occupants_user_idx                | CREATE INDEX estate_unit_occupants_user_idx ON public.estate_unit_occupants USING btree (estate_id, user_id)                                                                           |
+-----------------------+-----------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
(6 rows)

